447387 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447462 1075 #edb/ref 17592186447396 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447462 1075 #edb/ref 17592186447406 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447462 1075 #edb/ref 17592186447411 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447462 1075 #edb/ref 17592186447446 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447462 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447462 1077 "selection" 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447462 1078 #edb/ref 17592186447396 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447462 1079 #uuid "f3d617a6-eddf-5ce1-9bc2-1a0a23e70cdf" 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447463 1068 #edb/ref 17592186447452 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447463 1069 "q-151135" 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447463 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447463 1071 "![](images/c8/c8ccf0d2e4caded084951a0c99f4ca40a18bff31d4d8b09dfe2fe74ac2bc3bf2.png)\n\nList all of the perpendicular lines in the diagram above." 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447463 1072 #uuid "098eea8f-65a3-53e7-b532-eec2a5a08b22" 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447463 1074 "![](images/6a/6ac6e5de7f036c121f7a7f85d872faddb1010b120497bb18c1f03200443247a6.png)\n\nTwo lines are perpendicular if they intersect and form a ${90}^{∘}$ angle.\n\nIn the given diagram, the only perpendicular lines are $a$ and $b.$" 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447464 1068 #edb/ref 17592186447458 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447464 1069 "q-151142" 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447464 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447464 1071 "![](images/09/0927f7a957a2a5d8b91aafd71e488ce535f2c8ada2ef97d0592d58b75cd2eece.png)\n\nFrom the diagram above, which of the following statements is true?" 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447464 1072 #uuid "1f0a9542-3ba4-5c20-945c-8b2a173ef94b" 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447464 1074 "Suppose $a$ and $b$ are two lines. Then,\n\n- $a∥b$ means $a$ and $b$ are parallel, and\n\n- $a⊥b$ means $a$ and $b$ are perpendicular.\n\nIn the given diagram, there are two pairs of perpendicular lines:\n\n- $s$ is perpendicular to $t,$ which we write as $s⊥t$\n\n- $w$ is perpendicular to $t,$ which we write as $w⊥t.$\n\n![](images/75/756f579f20695c46394e6667fd78444504b1470619ea6ca4b68eed87eeed934e.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct statement is $s⊥t$ and $w⊥t.$" 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447465 1068 #edb/ref 17592186447457 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447465 1069 "q-37353" 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447465 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447465 1071 "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447465 1072 #uuid "243cda6a-277e-5555-a0d1-a4b1a66521e4" 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447465 1074 "First, we find the matrix $\\,A-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}5-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -1-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 4-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -3 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(A-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nSince the determinant of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix is given by the product of the entries on the main diagonal, we obtain the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}5-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -1-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 4-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -3 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (5-\\lambda )(-1-\\lambda )(4-\\lambda )(1-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -5)(\\lambda +1)(\\lambda -4)(\\lambda -1) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447466 1068 #edb/ref 17592186447454 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447466 1069 "q-153412" 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447466 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447466 1071 "![](images/e8/e8caa8e283c60d845c4b8fbe2c352818d300b51748f37b9788eac0bf1e73b7d5.png)\n\nIn the figure above, find the perpendicular sides." 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447466 1072 #uuid "2d6731a9-4b1d-5a58-8690-9d08ea615462" 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447466 1074 "Two lines are perpendicular if they intersect and form a ${90}^{∘}$ angle.\n\nFirst, notice that we have two sets of perpendicular lines:\n\n- $\\overset{⟷}{PU}$ is perpendicular to $\\overset{⟷}{PQ}$\n\n- $\\overset{⟷}{RS}$ is perpendicular to $\\overset{⟷}{ST}$\n\n![](images/24/2492594432bf29b2753d646c53b66ffd6230c21db71c4dd12479c9811217dc91.png)\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the sides $\\overset{―}{UP}$ and $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ are perpendicular, and $\\overset{―}{RS}$ and $\\overset{―}{ST}$ are also perpendicular. We can write this as follows:\n\n$\\,$ $\\overset{―}{UP}⊥\\overset{―}{PQ}$ and $\\overset{―}{RS}⊥\\overset{―}{ST}$" 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447467 1068 #edb/ref 17592186447450 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447467 1069 "q-151183" 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447467 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447467 1071 "![](images/fa/fa8cae4093f218e9df7859a1eb0ebf036b1d07fd7963042b8d66557f6842ccd6.png)\n\nList all of the parallel lines in the diagram above." 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447467 1072 #uuid "5b9ce7e4-46a6-59bd-8550-ab45a107e732" 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447467 1074 "![](images/40/4095a3e6206ed53b49eb411ef3b7a279bfa68e68bdd0abafa624161f78bc11cb.png)\n\nTwo lines are parallel if they never intersect.\n\nIn the given diagram, the only parallel lines are $l$ and $m.$" 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447468 1068 #edb/ref 17592186447461 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447468 1069 "q-153263" 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447468 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447468 1071 "![](images/de/de307da2bc912e9eb6f7312a16be40908d6ccd43cbc613367d042ed55090f2ee.png)\n\nGiven the diagram above, which of the following statements is true?" 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447468 1072 #uuid "838db218-c7b5-5ab1-b5e1-0abd38558574" 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447468 1074 "Suppose $p$ and $q$ are two lines. Then,\n\n- $p∥q$ means $p$ and $q$ are parallel, and\n\n- $p⊥q$ means $p$ and $q$ are perpendicular.\n\nThe lines $a,c$ and $b,d$ are parallel since they will never intersect. Therefore, the correct statement is $a∥c$ and $b∥d.$" 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447469 1068 #edb/ref 17592186447455 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447469 1069 "q-151168" 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447469 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447469 1071 "![](images/94/940a6996800ee85745643b34e429bb1fa85064bbab94f52bed328b074024fd22.png)\n\nIn the figure above, find the perpendicular sides." 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447469 1072 #uuid "86e173f6-09d0-539e-96a4-71b8b3120bde" 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447469 1074 "Two lines are perpendicular if they intersect and form a ${90}^{∘}$ angle.\n\nFirst, notice that the lines $\\overset{⟷}{EA}$ and  $\\overset{⟷}{AB}$ are perpendicular.\n\n![](images/81/81e84f9f6f3f50f6a5ef3f39381ebce028ccb52fa09b2d7042c9206a7027f337.png)\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the sides $\\overset{―}{EA}$ and $\\overset{―}{AB}$ are perpendicular. We can write this as follows: \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{EA}⊥\\overset{―}{AB}\n$$" 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447470 1068 #edb/ref 17592186447459 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447470 1069 "q-37357" 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447470 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447470 1071 "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix \n$B=[\\begin{aligned}-40 & 6 & 30 \\\\ 0 & -10 & 0 \\\\ -80 & 14 & 60\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447470 1072 #uuid "a82c548a-99d5-5982-b67f-c8bf62fc70fb" 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447470 1074 "First, we find the matrix $\\,B-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nB-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}-40-\\lambda  & 6 & 30 \\\\ 0 & -10-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ -80 & 14 & 60-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(B-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nExpanding the determinant across the $2$nd row, we obtain the following:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-40-\\lambda  & 6 & 30 \\\\ 0 & -10-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ -80 & 14 & 60-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-10-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}-40-\\lambda  & 30 \\\\ -80 & 60-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-10-\\lambda )((-40-\\lambda )(60-\\lambda )-(30)(-80)) & =0 \\\\ (-10-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-20\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +10)(\\lambda )(\\lambda -20) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda (\\lambda +10)(\\lambda -20) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447471 1068 #edb/ref 17592186447462 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447471 1069 "q-151162" 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447471 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447471 1071 "![](images/49/495da285b0971f050ad2baa2031ef27a9d9fd719078f535559cb2795057516de.png)\n\nIn the figure above, find the perpendicular sides." 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447471 1072 #uuid "b26db26d-7241-5602-a20a-a5953a1b2569" 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447471 1074 "Two lines are perpendicular if they intersect and form a ${90}^{∘}$ angle.\n\nFirst, notice that the lines $\\overset{⟷}{PQ}$ and  $\\overset{⟷}{TP}$ are perpendicular.\n\n![](images/db/db4497b62f456afacd78221d68a76200d18dedcfd1e3e7b73f64847e39a55ae9.png)\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the sides $\\overset{―}{TP}$ and $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ are perpendicular. We can write this as follows: \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{TP}⊥\\overset{―}{PQ}\n$$" 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447472 1068 #edb/ref 17592186447460 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447472 1069 "q-80553" 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447472 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447472 1071 "Determine all real eigenvalues $\\lambda $ of the matrix \n$B=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447472 1072 #uuid "bca3e3e8-22f6-5c69-8cd2-18d06e6e998f" 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447472 1074 "First, we find the matrix $\\,B-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nB-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}-3-\\lambda  & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -4-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(B-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nSince the determinant of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix is given by the product of the entries on the main diagonal, we obtain the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-3-\\lambda  & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -4-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-3-\\lambda )(-4-\\lambda )(5-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +3)(\\lambda +4)(\\lambda -5) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are ${\\lambda }_{1}=-3,$ $\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=-4,$ and ${\\lambda }_{3}=5.$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvalues of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix are always the entries on the main diagonal." 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447473 1068 #edb/ref 17592186447453 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447473 1069 "q-86751" 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447473 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447473 1071 "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix \n$E=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 7 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 4 & 2\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447473 1072 #uuid "d00c6bd7-a884-5180-8cfd-0ffa34fc590f" 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447473 1074 "First, we find the matrix $\\,E-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nE-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -2-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 7-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 4 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(E-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nSince the determinant of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix is given by the product of the entries on the main diagonal, we obtain the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(E-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -2-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 7-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 4 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )(-2-\\lambda )(7-\\lambda )(2-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -1)(\\lambda +2)(\\lambda -7)(\\lambda -2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447474 1068 #edb/ref 17592186447451 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447474 1069 "q-151165" 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447474 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447474 1071 "![](images/d8/d8af8bd4c928216d30d6ee1764139a86af1f7ac2ce6a01d9b98cb081a60ed322.png)\n\nIn the figure above, find the perpendicular sides." 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447474 1072 #uuid "e371cbf5-7ac9-5e8f-8f0f-f99fbc339fe5" 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447474 1074 "Two lines are perpendicular if they intersect and form a ${90}^{∘}$ angle.\n\nFirst, notice that we have two sets of perpendicular lines:\n\n- $\\overset{⟷}{AB}$ is perpendicular to $\\overset{⟷}{BC}$\n\n- $\\overset{⟷}{EA}$ is perpendicular to $\\overset{⟷}{AB}$\n\n![](images/90/90902346a26d5120e13c3df8e841e4fb57c6006b6e6a4390e30c6ae41f18630c.png)\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the sides $\\overset{―}{AB}$ and $\\overset{―}{BC}$ are perpendicular, and $\\overset{―}{EA}$ and $\\overset{―}{AB}$ are also perpendicular. We can write this as follows:\n\n$\\,$ $\\overset{―}{AB}⊥\\overset{―}{BC}$ and $\\overset{―}{EA}⊥\\overset{―}{AB}$" 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447475 1068 #edb/ref 17592186447456 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447475 1069 "q-153499" 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447475 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447475 1071 "![](images/86/8666a8c28b50deb88fc9e7cca3951b9d5fab9d8d07ede6abac774f41271324b5.png)\n\nIn the figure above, find the parallel sides." 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447475 1072 #uuid "f045e30a-5c77-5aee-853f-bedc4016f900" 13194139534999 17592186045417 true] [17592186447475 1074 "Two lines are parallel if they never intersect.\n\nNow, let's examine the direction of the sides in the figure to determine whether any pair lies along parallel lines.\n\nNotice that the sides $\\overset{―}{AB}$ and $\\overset{―}{DE}$ both lie along horizontal lines. The remaining sides have different directions, so they do not form any additional pair of parallel sides.\n\n![](images/7f/7f55b88378fe0e9389ea7a540cc40a02c9e619854a6815e9700b808770fa3a13.png)\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the sides $\\overset{―}{AB}$ and $\\overset{―}{DE}$ are parallel. We can write this as follows: \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{AB}∥\\overset{―}{DE}\n$$" 13194139534999 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-021593cc-5b62-54fd-ad2a-d326a2e3d10e" 17592186447375 "answer-040615ac-cb0a-5fce-99f6-4ed63d75aaeb" 17592186447376 "answer-0902d2e8-4185-5d65-b096-6b9e2ba9dd42" 17592186447377 "answer-09eda0ec-8e1b-5e11-a68f-03dfb4b379e2" 17592186447378 "answer-0dd806b5-b00a-5419-b12d-acd06881a066" 17592186447379 "answer-10a27dbc-011d-5655-9c47-5a5c5aad3533" 17592186447380